    "raw_text": "Gaydos Announces School Safety, Mental Health Grants for the 44th District\nAugust 14, 2026\nHARRISBURG\n- Rep. Valerie Gaydos (R-Allegheny) today announced school districts in the 44th Legislative District will be receiving a combined $699,456 in School Safety and Mental Health Grants through the Pennsylvania Commission on Crime and Delinquency’s School Safety and Security Committee (PCCD).\nThe funding will help local schools strengthen physical security and provide behavioral health support for students and staff.\n“Keeping our students safe and supporting their mental health must always be a priority,” said Gaydos. “These grants give our local school districts the resources they need to address safety concerns, strengthen security and support the well-being of students and staff. I’m pleased to see this funding coming directly back to our communities.”\nThe 44th District schools receiving funding are:\n•\nMoon Area School District – $276,692.\n•\nQuaker Valley School District – $175,545.\n•\nWest Allegheny School District – $247,219.\nThe PCCD’s School Safety and Security Committee administers programs designed to improve school safety and security, strengthen behavioral health supports, and provide training and technical assistance to schools across Pennsylvania.\nRepresentative Valerie Gaydos\n44th Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Rick Leiner\n717.260.6437\nrleiner@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
